# Git on Windows checks text files out with CRLF unless told otherwise, and an
# SVG counts as text. That is not harmless here: scripts/build-icons.mjs hashes
# logo.svg to prove the committed icons were generated from it, so the same
# logo hashed differently on Windows and `--ensure` refused to package. Every
# other job in that run passed; only win32-x64 failed, which is the signature.
#
# Line endings carry no meaning in an image. Keep them as committed.
*.svg text eol=lf
